#!/bin/sh
# Lance PR Radar et ouvre le navigateur.
set -e
cd "$(dirname "$0")"
PORT="${PORT:-4321}"
# /api/boot answers at once and only a PR Radar answers it, unlike / on a port taken by another app.
radar_up() { curl -sf "http://localhost:$PORT/api/boot" 2>/dev/null | grep -q '"boot"'; }
tab_open() { curl -sf "http://localhost:$PORT/api/boot" 2>/dev/null | grep -q '"tabs":[1-9]'; }
# A tab left open reconnects to a fresh server within a second or two: give it the time
# before opening another.
TAB_WAIT=0
if radar_up; then
  echo "PR Radar tourne déjà sur le port $PORT."
else
  node server.js &
  SERVER=$!
  until radar_up; do
    kill -0 "$SERVER" 2>/dev/null || exit 1
    sleep 0.3
  done
  TAB_WAIT=10
fi
until tab_open || [ "$TAB_WAIT" -le 0 ]; do
  sleep 0.5
  TAB_WAIT=$((TAB_WAIT - 1))
done
if tab_open; then
  echo "Un onglet PR Radar est déjà ouvert."
else
  open "http://localhost:$PORT/"
fi
wait
